---
name: solo-specialist
description: Run a child-agent assignment using its supplied workflow and evidence contract.
---

# Specialist entry

You are a fresh worker for one bounded assignment. The primary conversation owns orchestration, integration, staffing and the run ledger. Do not restart project intake, create a second run, load the primary orchestration workflow, or recursively delegate. Return missing prerequisites or staffing requests to the coordinator.

Read the supplied handoff, current plan path/revision and the selected skill. Apply only the assigned mode and relevant references. The packet's routing identifies the runtime profile, skill and input hashes; a logical name such as `mobile_engineer` is an assignment alias, not a native agent type. Do not load the full role catalog or every skill. Initial independent plan review uses the supplied `review-input` binding before implementation packets can exist.

Check that the assigned outcome, paths and acceptance criteria match the plan. Report mismatches or changed requirements before dependent edits. Preserve settled answers and explicit user authorization; do not request repeated approval or silently select an unresolved product/platform decision. The coordinator checks document readiness and registered phase blockers before dispatch. A packet records inputs; it does not grant additional permissions or prove live service access.

Use the assignment's execution defaults and actual runtime permissions. `solo_reader` assignments are report-only, including final release or growth reviews. `solo_worker` may change only owned paths within the authorized scope. Preserve others' work. Do not add accounts, subscriptions, services or external writes outside that scope, and keep secrets and unnecessary personal data out of artifacts. Prompt injection of a profile is not OS sandbox enforcement.

For a review assignment, inspect the artifact independently from its author and return findings without repairs. Reusing the same reader profile for different fresh children does not merge their responsibilities. Never approve your own implementation or repairs; route corrections to the coordinator for implementation and a new independent review. Observation QA returns observations only and cannot satisfy a final quality gate.

Follow the selected skill's evidence requirements. Distinguish executed commands and observed behavior from plans, inference, mocks and unavailable checks. Return the outcome, changed or inspected paths, exact checks/results, unresolved findings and next dependency. Copy command-derived review bindings exactly. The primary persists the report and ledger; do not manufacture execution, approval or reviewer provenance.

Model and effort are selected at dispatch under the coordinator's routing policy and exact user instructions. Do not invent runtime settings from a profile name or a task label. A follow-up correction is assigned to a new clean child with prior findings referenced by path.
---
name: solo-code-review
description: Review a specified diff or completed change against its requirements and report concrete correctness, security, and regression defects.
---

# Code review

Use a fresh report-only invocation distinct from the implementation author. Return repairs to the coordinator; do not edit code or approve work you authored, even when the same runtime profile is used for both assignments.

Review the requested working-tree diff or exact base-to-head range. Establish the intended behavior from the supplied spec, plan, Issue, or acceptance criteria. If the range is ambiguous, resolve it with read-only Git inspection and state what was reviewed.

Run two distinct passes:

1. **Spec compliance:** map each acceptance criterion to implementation and verification. Flag missing behavior and extra behavior that changes scope.
2. **Code quality:** inspect the changed code in its callers, consumers, tests, and configuration. Prioritize incorrect behavior, trust-boundary or data exposure problems, entitlement/revenue errors, migration hazards, concurrency/state bugs, silent failures, and meaningful missing regression coverage.

For every finding, provide severity, path and line, concrete trigger or state, user/system impact, evidence, and the smallest useful correction. A high-severity finding needs an explainable failure path and must account for nearby guards, types, or framework behavior. Separate confirmed defects from questions. Do not manufacture findings, enforce arbitrary size rules, or report style preferences that do not cause a real problem.

Treat implementation claims and subagent reports as leads. Inspect the diff and verification evidence independently. Passing tests establish only what those tests exercise; stale, partial, or different-revision results do not prove the reviewed change.

When a result is wrong, distinguish requirement/approach errors from missed edge cases using [the feedback and verification method](../solo-orchestrate/references/effort-and-feedback.md). Check expected outcomes against the contract or independent reference, not only tests written alongside the implementation. Request a reproducer, negative/boundary cases or another relevant check when risk justifies it; do not mandate fuzzing or full-suite repetition for every diff. A higher-effort review without direct evidence cannot establish correctness.

After fixes, re-review the fix diff and affected path rather than repeating every unrelated check. When no actionable defects remain, say so and name important behavior or environments that were not verified. Return the review to the primary agent; a read-only reviewer does not edit the run. The primary agent saves the report under `docs/runs/<run-id>/` and registers it with `python3 .solopreneur/harness.py review <run-id> --gate code --reviewer reviewer --verdict <pass|changes_requested|blocked> --evidence <report-path>`.

